{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_l4y4i4t753xfk5x7ggjddid43uj5bj5q2gnftllahepqwlufqlmq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass in both cargo profiles.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` symbol diff is **empty**. Both `.so`s export exactly `{bad, driver, good, printIntLine, printLine}`; the `static` helpers `goodG2B`/`goodB2G` are correctly absent from both. `ldd -r` shows zero unresolved imports. Nothing was missing, so nothing needed translating or stubbing.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all 34 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass across randomized inputs (fixed seed), ~5000 calls.\n- [x] **Phase C** — all 12 `ERRORS.md` rows + 8 generic FFI boundary rows have passing tests.\n- [x] **Every feature combination** — `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table (asserted by a test, not just prose), so the sole combination is the default; run under both `dev` and `release` (`release` sets `panic=\"abort\"` + optimization, which changes the Rust frame layout).\n\n**62 tests, 0 failures**, driven entirely through `dlopen`+`dlsym` on both `.so`s — the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are under test.\n\n## The one real finding\n\n`bad()` is a CWE-121 overflow: `buffer[data] = 1` with only a lower-bound check. I disassembled the C to derive exactly where each index lands (`buffer` at `-0x30(%rbp)`):\n\n| `data` | target | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `0..=9` | `buffer` | in bounds |\n| `10` | frame padding | benign |\n| `11` | **the loop counter `i`** | benign — `for` re-initializes it |\n| `12..=13` | **saved `rbp`** | caller's frame pointer destroyed |\n| `14..=15` | **return address** | fatal on `ret` |\n| `>=16` | caller's frame upward | corrupts whoever is above |\n\nMy first Phase B run failed on two rows, and the failures pointed in **opposite directions**: C dies at `bad(12)` where Rust survives; Rust dies at `bad(134)` where C survives. The crash sets also shift with call depth (`bad(d)` vs `driver(7,d)`). That's gcc's `-O0` frame layout, not program semantics — unreproducible by any translation, and it would change if `c_src` were rebuilt at `-O2`.\n\nSo I did **not** contort the Rust to fake a segfault at indices 12–15. Instead I narrowed the byte-exact-status domain to what's actually well-defined (`INT_MIN..=11`) and proved the strongest real property for `data >= 12`: I found the \"output difference\" at `bad(14)` was a *stdio artifact* — the ten lines were written but lost in the block-buffered pipe when the process died. With `setvbuf(stdout, NULL, _IONBF, 0)` before the call, **what the library prints is byte-identical across the entire `12..=400` region**, and far-out indices kill both. That's documented with measurements in `UB.md`, and it's the honest boundary of the claim rather than a hidden exclusion.\n\n## Guarding against vacuous tests\n\nGreen tests prove nothing if they can't fail, so I injected 18 mutants into `src/lib.rs` one at a time — **all 18 caught** (off-by-one in `goodB2G`'s bound, `out-of-bounds`→`out of bounds`, `%d`→`%u`, `goodG2B`'s hard-coded `7`→`3`, swapped call order, dropped NULL guard, and *adding* the missing bound check to `bad`). Two mutants initially looked like they \"survived\"; both were artifacts of my harness (one regex never applied, one mutant didn't compile and my failure counter misread that as a pass) — worth flagging since that failure mode silently inflates mutation scores.\n\n`src/lib.rs` was restored and verified **md5-identical** to the original; `c_src/` sources retain their checkout mtimes and sizes, with only `c_src/build/` added by cmake.\n\nOne note: `crates.io` is unreachable from the sandbox, so I added `translation/.cargo/config.toml` with `offline = true` (libloading 0.8.9 was already in the local registry cache). Drop that file if you build somewhere with network access."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1032,"cache_read_input_tokens":143641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1032,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"508d9285-f2f8-4563-9ede-ba90eaf98e51","uuid":"e6b80938-adf9-4182-b85d-93c83e83f6e8","timestamp":"2026-08-28T11:47:50.524Z"}
